        "original_id": "c2304010-3513-501e-9ef1-ba450736bf97",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert M. Fomon\n- Organizations: E. F. Hutton & Co., New York Stock Exchange, Pacific Stock Exchange\n- Places: 11 Wall Street, Lower Manhattan, New York City, New York\n- Roles: Chairman, Chief Executive Officer, governor, Chairman of the Board of Governors\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Michael Fomon was born on January 3, 1925, and died on May 31, 2000.\n- Robert Michael Fomon was an American financier.\n- Robert Michael Fomon served as Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of E. F. Hutton & Co. from 1970 to 1987.\n- Robert Michael Fomon was a governor of the New York Stock Exchange.\n- Robert Michael Fomon was Chairman of the Board of Governors of the Pacific Stock Exchange.\n- The New York Stock Exchange is an American stock exchange.\n- The New York Stock Exchange is abbreviated as NYSE and nicknamed \"The Big Board.\"\n- The New York Stock Exchange is located at 11 Wall Street in Lower Manhattan, New York City, New York.",
